//! The `Syscalls` trait with one immediate-or-deferred method per syscall, the request enum, the `Layered` adapter,
//! user-memory reference types, result and restart types, and the return-to-guest interface.
//!
//! Everything above the kernel talks to it only through this crate. The trait, the request enum
//! and the adapter are generated by `wasixv2-codegen` from `lib/wasixv2/codegen/wit`; see the
//! header of `src/generated.rs`.
//!
//! On syscall returns and preemption points exec checks the task's WorkFlag once. When raised,
//! it awaits Control::run_task_work with the current Caller before draining take_pending's
//! signals/actions. This is the kernel's memory-bearing task_work_run boundary; a notification
//! wakes interruptible calls without fabricating a signal, using their normal restart policy.
//!
//! `UserMemory::read` and `write` are kernel user copies, like Linux's `copy_from_user` and
//! `copy_to_user` (`include/linux/uaccess.h`): a nonempty copy into or out of the low guard
//! faults even when its host pages remain readable. The guest's own loads are a separate path
//! and may read that guard for LLVM's null-va_list compatibility. `force_read` is the kernel's
//! internal access to host-readable bytes, not a user-copy validation bypass for syscalls.
//!
//! `UserMemory::layout` is an optional host-side contract for separate Linux brk and top-down
//! mmap arenas. `MemoryLayout` identifies the immutable image/data bounds, initial break,
//! maximum, and execution-owned reservations. Its default `None` preserves allocation by
//! linear-memory growth for existing embedders; it does not change the guest syscall ABI.

